 "intro": {
  "text": "The Italian Game begins 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4: both sides push the pawn in front of the king two squares and bring out a knight, and then White's bishop comes out to c4. From there it points at f7, the pawn beside Black's king that only the king defends. After 3...Bc5, Black's bishop to c5, you push the c-pawn to c3 to get ready for the d-pawn to come to d4, so that two pawns stand side by side in the centre, and you castle as soon as it is safe."
 },
